tomas: Heads-up from pairing with two new hires today  a few README snippets are causing runtime errors rather than auth 401s. Noticed three patterns: TypeScript default import vs named import, top-level await in Node examples (breaks older Node), and a stray `Token:` header in a curl example.

anya: Oof. Any samples I can patch quickly?

tomas: Yep. Examples: 1) TypeScript quickstart: `import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'` then `new Redwood.Client(...)` throws because our TS SDK exports named Client, not a default. 2) Node async example uses top-level `await` without instructing folks to run `node --harmony-top-level-await` or use an async IIFE. Lots of newcomers run Node 16 and paste it straight in. 3) curl in README uses `-H "Token: $REDWOOD_API_KEY"` (we use `Authorization: Bearer ...`).

frank: Can you paste the problematic snippets?

 t o m a s: Sure, found in quickstart.md and sample-app README: broken TS snippet:
```ts
// broken (default import)
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.Client({ token: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
await client.generate({ model: 'stable-001', prompt: 'hi' });
```

Correct TS snippet (named import + top-level await note):
```ts
// correct
import { Client } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Client({ token: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
// If your Node doesn't support top-level await, wrap this in async IIFE
(async () => {
  await client.generate({ model: 'stable-001', prompt: 'hi' });
})();
```

And the curl fix:
```bash
# bad
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H "Token: $REDWOOD_API_KEY" -d '{"prompt":"hi"}'
# good
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_API_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"prompt":"hi"}'
```

anya: Nice catch. We should also avoid `sk-` literals and mention env var rotation best practice (don't check tokens into dotfiles).

marvin: For TS we should add a tiny Build/Run note at top of quickstart: supported Node versions (>=18) and advise using `npx ts-node` or async IIFE. That reduces friction.

frank: Also found a Rust example that does `Redwood::new("sk-...")`  our Rust SDK accepts a `Config::from_env()` pattern now. Small sweep to update patterns across sample-apps would help.

docs-bot: Reminder: PRs that touch >5 READMEs need an entry in docs-change-log.md and a docs owner approval. Also run the docs grep for `Token:` and top-level `await` in codeblocks.

tomas: I'll open a single PR to: update TS import, add top-level await guidance, replace `Token:`/`sk-` literals, update Rust/Go snippets to use env-driven construction, and add a short "Common gotchas" section. I'll tag @anya and @frank for review.

anya: Can we add a docs CI job to flag `import Redwood from` (TS default import) and `Token:` header strings? Quick grep found 4 occurrences each.

marvin: Filed issue #4588 for the docs linter rules + CI job. I'll own the Node version note and the quick start change.

frank: Thanks — these are small changes but will save new devs a lot of time. :seedling:
